### VietPay — Wallet flows (wallet-service via Traefik, JWT-protected)
### Run `login` first; wallet calls read the token inline via
### {{login.response.body.accessToken}}. (IntelliJ: use ...body.$.accessToken)

@baseUrl = http://localhost
@email = test2@vietpay.dev
@password = Password123!

### Login to obtain an access token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Create a wallet (USD) -> 201
# @name createWallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Get the wallet balance -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Unsupported currency -> 422 (valid ISO but not offered)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "KWD"
}

### Malformed currency -> 400 (not a real ISO code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "US"
}

### Unknown wallet -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### No token -> 401 (Traefik ForwardAuth rejects before wallet-service)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009
